+The relay refuses to start when the file is missing or unreadable, a required key is absent, a value is
+malformed or out of range, or a key is not recognised. It prints `Refusing to start: <reason>` to standard
+error and exits with status `2`. An omitted optional key uses its default; a key that is present with a bad
+value never does.
+
 ## Tests
 
     java tools/RunTests.java
 
 The runner compiles `src/main/java` and `src/test/java` and runs every JUnit 5 test. It needs
 `lib/junit-platform-console-standalone.jar`.
